PASS 3/3 :: BIRTH

This PR converts the three-pass reconstruction into an executable boundary instead of another architecture-only checkpoint.

Adds `platform/packages/cognitive-compiler/` with:
- a minimal self-compile kernel contract;
- deterministic capability-based organ selection;
- explicit capability gaps instead of fabricated execution;
- proof/falsification gates separating tool success from task success;
- candidate-only mutation creation so corrections cannot silently rewrite the kernel;
- birth fixtures covering visual organ dispatch, missing capabilities, unsupported success claims, and mutation promotion boundaries.

Core invariant: `MondayID != state`; MondayID is the law that reconstructs, executes, verifies, and evolves state.

This intentionally does not claim deployment or autonomous background execution. It establishes a testable runtime boundary on top of the existing platform embodiment branch.

Canonical closure synchronization for the already-merged P7.06-UI2 implementation (PR #56).

Closure evidence:
- implementation PR #56 merged at `a22ba781d32f64b7097aeaf05a90651308533811`;
- exact reviewed implementation head `305faafb790e1387cac2aaafa348fbc4ac583797`;
- five functional review/revise iterations closed all material implementation objections;
- Reference Python CI #107 / `32159051764` passed on the exact implementation head;
- closure synchronization itself was applied only after full Reference Python CI #108 / `32162204861` passed, followed by asserted exact-text replacements and `git diff --check`;
- final PR diff contains only four canonical documentation files: the UI2 functional-review record, live-workspace substream, active Phase 7 and sole canonical ROADMAP.

Disposition:
- mark `P7.06-UI2 = Complete / PASS` only for its bounded repository implementation/review scope;
- advance `P7.06-UI` to 50% with `P7.06-UI3 — Persistent private operator access` current;
- preserve UI4 as the first real selected-owner interaction proof;
- no lifecycle/Product Contract/Production/public-interface/browser-support/SLA promotion.

Temporary patch machinery was self-removed and is absent from the final PR diff.
